        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e3a7343f-c747-5edd-96f2-cf4c6b33bae6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lady Alexandra Naldera Curzon, George Curzon, Mary Victoria Curzon\n- Roles: 1st Marquess Curzon of Kedleston, Viceroy of India, Baroness Curzon of Kedleston, British Conservative statesman\n\nFacts:\n- George Nathaniel Curzon was born on 11 January 1859 and died on 20 March 1925.\n- George Curzon was known as The Lord Curzon of Kedleston from 1898 to 1911 and as The Earl Curzon of Kedleston from 1911 to 1921.\n- George Curzon was the 1st Marquess Curzon of Kedleston, a British Conservative statesman, and Viceroy of India.\n- Lady Alexandra Naldera Curzon was born on 20 March or April 1904 and died on 7 August 1995.\n- Lady Alexandra Curzon was the third daughter of George Curzon and his first wife, Mary Victoria Curzon.\n- Mary Victoria Curzon was an American mercantile heiress and Baroness Curzon of Kedleston, and her maiden name was Leiter.",
